Fix for clingox UPSTREAM-ISSUES U35: grounding an #external with an arithmetic
type term crashes the process.

ExternalHeadAtom::rewriteArithmetics calls Term::rewriteArithmetics on the atom
and on the type term and throws away the returned replacement. For a BinOpTerm
that is not linear (X\2, X**2, X+X) and for a UnOpTerm other than NEG (|X|, ~X)
the call moves the operands into the term it registers in the arithmetics map
and returns the auxiliary variable that must take the term's place. Discarded,
the original term stays in the statement with null children, and the next
traversal (Statement::check) dereferences them: SIGSEGV from any program text
such as "#external e(X) : f(X). [X\2]". Every other caller wraps the call in
Term::replace; this patch does the same. The unsafe-variable check then sees
the auxiliary variable, so an unbound X is reported as an ordinary error.

ProjectHeadAtom and HeuristicHeadAtom carry the same discarded call for their
atom. Neither is reachable today (the parser and the AST layer only produce
function atoms there), so the change keeps the three copies consistent.
Against clingo v5.8.2; suitable for upstream.

diff --git a/libgringo/src/input/aggregates.cc b/libgringo/src/input/aggregates.cc
index 39b40f3..76a9553 100644
--- a/libgringo/src/input/aggregates.cc
+++ b/libgringo/src/input/aggregates.cc
@@ -2542,7 +2542,7 @@
 }
 
 void ProjectHeadAtom::rewriteArithmetics(Term::ArithmeticsMap &arith, AuxGen &auxgen) {
-    atom_->rewriteArithmetics(arith, auxgen);
+    Term::replace(atom_, atom_->rewriteArithmetics(arith, auxgen));
 }
 
 void ProjectHeadAtom::assignLevels(AssignLevel &lvl) {
@@ -2627,8 +2627,8 @@
 }
 
 void ExternalHeadAtom::rewriteArithmetics(Term::ArithmeticsMap &arith, AuxGen &auxgen) {
-    atom_->rewriteArithmetics(arith, auxgen);
-    type_->rewriteArithmetics(arith, auxgen);
+    Term::replace(atom_, atom_->rewriteArithmetics(arith, auxgen));
+    Term::replace(type_, type_->rewriteArithmetics(arith, auxgen));
 }
 
 void ExternalHeadAtom::assignLevels(AssignLevel &lvl) {
@@ -2727,7 +2727,7 @@
 }
 
 void HeuristicHeadAtom::rewriteArithmetics(Term::ArithmeticsMap &arith, AuxGen &auxgen) {
-    atom_->rewriteArithmetics(arith, auxgen);
+    Term::replace(atom_, atom_->rewriteArithmetics(arith, auxgen));
 }
 
